---
import Article from "../../../layouts/Article.astro";
import KeyTakeaway from "../../../components/KeyTakeaway.astro";
import ComparisonTable from "../../../components/ComparisonTable.astro";
import GiftPick from "../../../components/GiftPick.astro";
import GiftFaq from "../../../components/GiftFaq.astro";
import ChristmasDelivery from "../../../components/ChristmasDelivery.astro";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What do you get a Scythe fan for Christmas?",
    a: "An upgrade for the copy they already play. 3D-printed resource tokens replace the plain wooden blocks on the map with sculpted wood, grain, metal and oil, and they're on the table for the whole game. If they mostly play two-player, Duel of Meloch is the new box to give.",
  },
  {
    q: "What's a good small gift for a Scythe player?",
    a: "The encounter tokens. They're inexpensive, they fit in a stocking, and the raised markers make every encounter spot visible from across the table, so encounters get contested more often.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is Duel of Meloch a good gift for someone who loves Scythe?",
    a: "Yes, if they own Scythe and often play with two. They get a 45-minute duel, plus Constantinople and the Adventurous mat, which both work in their normal Scythe games. For a group that always plays with three or more, the duel half won't get much use.",
  },
  {
    q: "Will a Scythe gift from Fjord Labs arrive before Christmas?",
    a: "Physical pieces are posted from Sweden within 3–5 business days. In mid-November, Etsy estimated 7–13 days to delivery in Europe and the UK and 9–15 days to the US, so order early in December at the latest, and earlier for the US.",
  },
];
---

<Article
  title="Scythe Gift Ideas: 7 Christmas Gifts for Scythe Fans (2026)"
  description="Christmas gifts for someone who loves Scythe: sculpted resource tokens, encounter tokens for a stocking, Duel of Meloch for two-player fans, and inserts that keep it tidy."
  game="scythe"
  gameTitle="Scythe"
  category="Guide"
  publishDate="2026-11-18"
>
  <p>
    Scythe players already own a beautiful game, so a good gift doesn't replace it.
    It makes the parts they handle every turn match the art on the box, or gives
    them a way to play Scythe on the nights the full game won't fit. Here are seven,
    from a stocking stuffer to the new two-player box.
  </p>

  <KeyTakeaway answer="The best gift for a Scythe fan is 3D-printed resource tokens: sculpted wood, grain, metal and oil instead of plain blocks on the map. Encounter tokens make the small gift, and if they mostly play two-player, Duel of Meloch (2026) is the box to give, with an insert to keep it tidy." />

  <h2>The upgrade they'll see all game</h2>
  <p>
    Scythe's resources sit on the map in front of everyone, all game. That's why
    generic blocks undersell it, and why this is the upgrade owners notice most.
  </p>

  <GiftPick
    slug="scythe-resource-tokens"
    label="Our top pick"
    note="Sculpted wood, grain, metal and oil that replace the wooden blocks on their territories. The board becomes readable at a glance, which matters in a game where you're always sizing up the other economies."
  />
  <GiftPick
    slug="hexagon-token-trays"
    note="Stackable hex bowls to keep the resource supply sorted beside the board. A cheap add-on if you're buying the tokens."
  />

  <h2>A small gift or stocking stuffer</h2>

  <GiftPick
    slug="scythe-encounter-tokens"
    label="Best small gift"
    note="Raised encounter markers that stand out on the map. Encounters get contested more often, so a small swap changes how the game plays, not just how it looks."
  />

  <h2>If they mostly play two-player: Duel of Meloch</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/games/duel-of-meloch/what-is-duel-of-meloch/">Scythe: Duel of Meloch</a> is
    Stonemaier's standalone two-player game from 2026. One player commands a Scythe
    faction, the other an Expeditions crew, and a game takes about 45 minutes. The box
    also contains Constantinople, a new Scythe faction, and the Adventurous player mat,
    and both work in normal Scythe. For a Scythe fan who rarely gets four players
    together, it covers the evenings the big game can't.
  </p>
  <p>
    Not sure it suits them? Our <a href="/games/duel-of-meloch/is-duel-of-meloch-worth-it/">honest
    look at whether Duel of Meloch is worth it</a> covers who it's for, and
    <a href="/games/duel-of-meloch/duel-of-meloch-vs-scythe/">Duel of Meloch vs Scythe</a>
    explains how the two differ.
  </p>
  <p>Already own it? These keep a game that's meant to be quick, quick to set up:</p>

  <GiftPick
    slug="duel-of-meloch-insert-lids"
    label="Our most complete insert"
    note="Lidded, nested trays in four colours, with a slot for the airship and a tray for sleeved cards. Everything drops back into the box and the lid closes flat."
  />
  <GiftPick
    slug="scythe-duel-of-meloch-insert"
    note="Lidded, stackable trays in the game's own colours that lock together, so the whole game lifts out in one stack. Good for a box that travels in a backpack."
  />

  <h2>If they want more Scythe</h2>
  <p>
    Scythe has five base factions, and the Invaders from Afar expansion adds two more
    along with seats for up to seven players. For a group that's played the base game
    to death, an expansion is the other classic gift. Our
    <a href="/games/scythe/faction-tier-list/">Scythe faction tier list</a> shows how
    the factions compare, including Constantinople from Duel of Meloch.
  </p>

  <h2>Which Scythe gift fits?</h2>

  <ComparisonTable>
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left p-3 bg-bark/[0.02] font-heading font-semibold text-bark/70">If they…</th>
          <th class="text-left p-3 bg-bark/[0.02] font-heading font-semibold text-bark/70">Give them</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Play Scythe regularly</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Resource tokens</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Need a small or stocking gift</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Encounter tokens</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Mostly play with two</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Duel of Meloch</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Already own Duel of Meloch</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">A Duel of Meloch insert</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Have a big group</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Invaders from Afar</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </ComparisonTable>

  <ChristmasDelivery />

  <GiftFaq heading="Scythe Christmas gift questions" faqs={faqs} />

  <p>
    Shopping for more than one gamer? Our
    <a href="/gifts/">gift guide for board gamers</a> covers other games, handmade
    pieces and gifts for every budget.
  </p>
</Article>
